    "title": "Vestavia Hills police announce several arrests following month-long investigation - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By AJ Holliday ,\n1 hours ago\nVESTAVIA HILLS, Ala. ( WIAT ) — The Vestavia Hills Police Department announced Tuesday the conclusion of a month-long investigation into suspected vehicle theft within the area.\nMobile County Sheriff Paul Burch, incumbent, wins Republican nomination in Alabama Primary Election Investigators said a combination of investigative techniques were used to identify people believed to be connected to an organized vehicle fraud operation. During the investigation, undercover investigators met with a suspect believed to be involved in the sale of vehicles with salvaged titles and inaccurate odometer readings.\nA residence being used to store vehicles suspected of being connected to the operation was identified. A search warrant was issued at locations in the 7000 block and the 2400 block of Colony Park Drive resulted in the recovery of vehicles and evidence related to the investigation.\nAlabama Primary Election Results 2026 (key race updates) The following people were arrested and charged with first-degree theft of property:\nAmar Serban Alondra Serban Ramona Serban Marius Serban Marian Dumitru Bernardo Mihai Police stated additional charges are pending.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
    "summary": "VESTAVIA HILLS, Ala. ( WIAT ) — The Vestavia Hills Police Department announced Tuesday the conclusion of a month-long investigation into suspected vehicle theft within the area. Mobile County Sheriff Paul Burch, incumbent, wins Republican nomination in Alabama Primary Election Investigators said a combination of investigative techniques were used to identify people believed to be connected to an organized vehicle fraud operation. During the investigation, undercover investigators met with a suspect believed to be involved in the sale of vehicles with salvaged titles and inaccurate odometer readings.",
